issue_description.code_example:
```tsx // File: src/features/calculator/Calculator.tsx, Lines 252-262 and 348-401
return { ...displayForm, weight: form.units === "metric" ? canonicalWeightKg : kilogramsToPounds(canonicalWeightKg), // ... };
// Entering 66.1 lb stores about 29.9825 kg here. canonicalWeightKg: current.units === "metric" ? Number(value) : poundsToKilograms(Number(value)),
// The switch displays the rounded value 30, but leaves canonicalWeightKg unchanged. weight: String( units === "imperial" ? convertWeightForDisplay(current.canonicalWeightKg, "metric-to-imperial") : convertWeightForDisplay(Number(current.weight), "imperial-to-metric"), ), ```
Reproduction:
1. Open `/calorie-calculator/`. 2. Change Units to `Imperial (lb, in)`. 3. Enter `66.1` in Weight. The field is valid and results remain visible. 4. Change Units to `Metric (kg, cm)`. 5. Observe Weight displays `30`, but it is marked invalid and the results are disabled.
